{
  "title": "22: al-Hajj الحج",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اتَّقُوْا رَبَّكُمْ‌ۚ اِنَّ زَلْزَلَةَ السَّاعَةِ شَىْءٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(1)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO TAQOO TAQUL INNAL ZALZALATA AS-SAAA’ATE SHAY-UN A’ZEEM.\nO’ ye People! Fear ye your Lord! Verily, the quake of the Hour (of Doom) is a thing tremendous!\nيَوْمَ تَرَوْنَهَا تَذْهَلُ كُلُّ مُرْضِعَةٍ عَمَّاۤ اَرْضَعَتْ وَتَضَعُ كُلُّ ذَاتِ حَمْلٍ حَمْلَهَا وَتَرَى النَّاسَ سُكٰرٰى وَمَا هُمْ بِسُكٰرٰى وَلٰكِنَّ عَذَابَ اللّٰهِ شَدِيْدٌ‏(2)\nYAWMA TARAWNAHAA TAZHALU KULLO MURZEA’ATIN A’MMAA AARZAA’AT WA TAZAA-O’ KULLO ZAATIL HAMLIN HAMLAHAA WA TARAL NAASA SUKAARAA WA MAA HUM BESUKAARAA LAAKINNAL A’ZAABAL LAAHE SHADEEDUN.\nOn the day ye shall behold it, every suckling mother shall forsake her suckling babe; and every pregnant female shall drop her load, and thou shalt behold the people (as) intoxicated; But the wrath of God will be (so) terrible.\nوَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يُّجَادِلُ فِى اللّٰهِ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ وَّيَتَّبِعُ كُلَّ شَيْطٰنٍ مَّرِيْدٍ ۙ‏(3)\nWA MENAN NAASE MAN YYUJAADELU FIL LAAHE BEGHAYRIL I’LMIN WWAYATTABEU’U KULLA SHAYTAANIR MMAREEDIN.\nAnd among the people there is he who disputeth about God without knowledge, and followeth every rebellious Satan,\nكُتِبَ عَلَيْهِ اَنَّهٗ مَنْ تَوَلَّاهُ فَاَنَّهٗ يُضِلُّهٗ وَيَهْدِيْهِ اِلٰى عَذَابِ السَّعِيْرِ‏(4)\nKOTEBA A’LAYHE ANNAHU MAN TAWALLAAHU FA ANNAHU YUZELLUH WAYAHDEEHE ELAA A’ZAABIN SA-E’ER.\nAgainst him is decreed that whosoever taketh him as his friend, then verily shall he beguile him and lead him unto the torment of the burning fire.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ فِىْ رَيْبٍ مِّنَ الْبَعْثِ فَاِنَّا خَلَقْنٰكُمْ مِّنْ تُرَابٍ ثُمَّ مِنْ نُّطْفَةٍ ثُمَّ مِنْ عَلَقَةٍ ثُمَّ مِنْ مُّضْغَةٍ مُّخَلَّقَةٍ وَّغَيْرِ مُخَلَّقَةٍ لِّنُبَيِّنَ لَكُمْ‌ ؕ وَنُقِرُّ فِى الْاَرْحَامِ مَا نَشَآءُ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى ثُمَّ نُخْرِجُكُمْ طِفْلًا ثُمَّ لِتَبْلُغُوْۤا اَشُدَّكُمْ ‌ۚ وَمِنْكُمْ مَّنْ يُّتَوَفّٰى وَمِنْكُمْ مَّنْ يُّرَدُّ اِلٰٓى اَرْذَلِ الْعُمُرِ لِكَيْلَا يَعْلَمَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ عِلْمٍ شَيْئًا‌ ؕ وَتَرَى الْاَرْضَ هَامِدَةً فَاِذَاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْهَا الْمَآءَ اهْتَزَّتْ وَرَبَتْ وَاَنْۢبَتَتْ مِنْ كُلِّ زَوْجٍۢ بَهِيْجٍ‏(5)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO IN KUNTUM FEE RAIBIM MENAL BA’SE WA FAINNAA KHALAQNAAKUM MIN TORAABIN SUMMA MIN NUTFATIN SUMMA MIN A’ALAQATIN SUMMA MIN MMUZGHATIN MMUKHALLAQATIN WWAGHAYRE MUKHALLAQATIN LLENUBAYNA LAKUM WANUQERRU FIL AL-AARHAAME MAA NASHAAA-O ELAA ELAA AJALIM SUMMA NUKHREJUKUM TEFLAN SUMMA LETABLUGHOOA AASHUDDAKUM WA MINKUM MAN YYUTAWAFFAA WA MINKUM MAN YYURADDU ELAA AARZALE AL-U’UMURE LE-KAYLAA YAA’LAMA MIN BA’DE I’LMIN SHAY-ANW WA TARAL ARZA HAAMEDATAN FA-EZAA ANZALNAA A’LAYHAA MAAA-AH TAZZAT WARABAT WA AMBATAT MIN KULLE ZAWJIN BAHEEJIN.\nO’ people! if ye be in doubt about (your) rising again (resurrection), then (reflect ye that) verily We created you from dust, then from sperm, then from a clot, then from a lump of flesh, formed and (sometimes) partly unformed, that we may manifest (our power) unto you, and We cause to stay in the womb what We will until an appointed term, then We bring ye forth as babes, then (foster you) that ye reach your maturity; and of you is he who is caused to die, and of you is he who is brought back to the feeblest (state of) old age that he knoweth not aught after knowing (much), and ye behold the earth dried, dead, but when send We down on it water, it is stirred (to life) and swelleth up and produceth every kind of attractive herbage (in pairs).\nذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الْحَقُّ وَاَنَّهٗ يُحْىِ الْمَوْتٰى وَاَنَّهٗ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ ۙ‏(6)\nZAA LEKA BE-ANNAL LAAHA HOWA HAQQO WA ANNAHU LAAHUL MAWTAA WA ANNAHU A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nThis is because Verily God, He is the Reality, and because verily He giveth life unto the dead, and because verily He, over all things hath power.\nوَّاَنَّ السَّاعَةَ اٰتِيَةٌ لَّا رَيْبَ فِيْهَا ۙ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَبْعَثُ مَنْ فِى الْقُبُوْرِ‏(7)\nWA ANNAL SAA-A’TA AAATEETUN LAA RAYBA FEEHAA WA ANNAL LAAHA YABA’ASU MAN FIL QOBOORE.\nAnd that the Hour (of Resurrection) is coming there is no doubt therein and that God will raise up those in the graves.\nوَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يُّجَادِلُ فِى اللّٰهِ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ وَّلَا هُدًى وَلَا كِتٰبٍ مُّنِيْرٍ ۙ‏(8)\nWA MENAN NAASE MAN YYUJAADELU FIL LAAHE BEGHAYRIL I’LMIN WA LAA HODAM WA LAA KETAABIM MMUNEERIN.\nAnd among the people there is he who disputeth about God without knowledge and without any guidance and without any enlightening book,\nثَانِىَ عِطْفِهٖ لِيُضِلَّ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ‌ؕ لَهٗ فِى الدُّنْيَا خِزْىٌ‌ وَّنُذِيْقُهٗ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ عَذَابَ الْحَرِيْقِ‏(9)\nSAANEAAA E’ETFEH LEEZELLA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE LAHU FIL DUNYAA KHIZYUN WWANUZEEQUH YAWMA QEYAAMATE A’ZAABAL AL-HAREEQE.\nTurning away haughtily that he may beguile (others) from the way of God; For him in this world is disgrace and We shall make him taste on the Day of Judgment the punishment of the burning (Hell fire)\nذٰ لِكَ بِمَا قَدَّمَتْ يَدٰكَ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ لَيْسَ بِظَلَّامٍ لِّلْعَبِيْدِ‏(10)\nZAA LEKA BEMAA QADDAMAT YADAAKA WA ANNAL LAAHA LAYSA BEZALLAAMIL LIL-A’BEED.\n(And unto him will be said): “This is for what sent before thy two hands, and that (verily) God is not unjust to His servants.\nوَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَّعْبُدُ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى حَرْفٍ‌ ‌ۚ فَاِنْ اَصَابَهٗ خَيْرٌ اۨطْمَاَنَّ بِهٖ‌ ۚ وَاِنْ اَصَابَتْهُ فِتْنَةُ اۨنقَلَبَ عَلٰى وَجْهِهٖ‌ۚ خَسِرَ الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةَ ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الْخُسْرَانُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(11)\nWA MENAN NAASE MAN YYAA’BUDU LAAHA A’LAA HARFIN FA-IN AASAABAH KHAYRUL ATMAANNA BEHI WA AASAABATHU FETNATU ANQALABA A’LAA WAJHEHI KHASERA DUNYAA WA AAKHERATA ZAA LEKA HOWA AL-KHUSRAANU MOBEEN.\nAnd of the people is he who worshippeth God (standing) on the verge, so if befalleth unto him good he is satisfied, and if afflicteth him a trial, he turneth back his face; loses he both this world and (also) the here after; That is a loss (which is) manifest.\nيَدْعُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَضُرُّهٗ وَمَا لَا يَنْفَعُهٗ ‌ؕ ذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الضَّلٰلُ الْبَعِيْدُ‌ ۚ‏(12)\nYAD-O’O MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAA YAZURRUH WA MAA LAA YANFAU’UH ZAA LEKA HOWA AZ-ZALAALU AL-BAE’EEDU.\nHe calleth besides God, that which harmeth him not nor doth it profit him; that is straying far off.\nيَدْعُوْا لَمَنْ ضَرُّهٗۤ اَقْرَبُ مِنْ نَّفْعِهٖ‌ؕ لَبِئْسَ الْمَوْلٰى وَلَبِئْسَ الْعَشِيْرُ‏(13)\nYAD-O’O LAMAN ZARRUH AQRABO MIN NNAFE’EH LABESA AL-MAWLAA WA LABESA AL-A’ASHEERU.\nHe calleth upon him whose hurt is nearer than his profit: verily evil is the lord, and evil certainly is the associate.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُدْخِلُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَفْعَلُ مَا يُرِيْدُ‏(14)\nINNAL LAAHA YUDKHELU LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO INNAL LAAHA YAF-A’LO MAA YOREEDO.\nVerily God will admit those who believe and do good deeds, into gardens ’neath which flow rivers; Verily God doeth what He intendeth.\nمَنْ كَانَ يَظُنُّ اَنْ لَّنْ يَّنْصُرَهُ اللّٰهُ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ فَلْيَمْدُدْ بِسَبَبٍ اِلَى السَّمَآءِ ثُمَّ لْيَقْطَعْ فَلْيَنْظُرْ هَلْ يُذْهِبَنَّ كَيْدُهٗ مَا يَغِيْظُ‏(15)\nMAN KAANA YAZUNNO AN LAN-Y YYANSURAHU LAAHO FIL DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH FALYAMDUD BESABABIN ELAL SAMAAA-E SUMMA LYAQTAA’ FALYANZUR HAL YUZHEBANNA KAYDUH MAA YAGHEEZU.\nWhoever thinketh that never will God help him (the Apostle Muhammad) in this life nor in the hereafter, let him stretch a cord unto the heaven (to raise himself) and hang himself, then let him cut it off, then see if his device taketh away what he is enraged at.\nوَكَذٰلِكَ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ اٰيٰتٍۢ بَيِّنٰتٍۙ وَّاَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَهْدِىْ مَنْ يُّرِيْدُ‏(16)\nWA KAZAALEKA ANZALNAAHO AAYAATIM BAYYENAAT WA ANNAL LAAHA YAHDEE MAN YYUREEDU.\nAnd thus have We sent it down, as signs manifest, and that verily God guideth whomsoever He intendeth.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَالَّذِيْنَ هَادُوْا وَالصّٰبِئِيْنَ وَالنَّصٰرٰى وَالْمَجُوْسَ وَالَّذِيْنَ اَشْرَكُوْۤا ‌ۖ  اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَفْصِلُ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ شَهِيْدٌ‏(17)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WAL LAZEENA HAADOO WAS SAABE-EENA WAN NASAARAA WAL MAJOOSA WAL LAZEENA ASHRAKOO INNAL LAAHA YAFSELU BAYNAHUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE INNAL LAAHA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN WA.\nVerily, those who believe and those who are Jews and the Sabaeans and the Christians and the Magians (Zoroastrians) those who associate (other gods with God), verily, God will decide between them on the Day of Judgment; Verily God is witness over all things.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَسْجُدُ لَهٗ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَالشَّمْسُ وَالْقَمَرُ وَالنُّجُوْمُ وَ الْجِبَالُ وَالشَّجَرُ وَالدَّوَآبُّ وَكَثِيْرٌ مِّنَ النَّاسِ‌ ؕ وَكَثِيْرٌ حَقَّ عَلَيْهِ الْعَذَابُ‌ؕ وَمَنْ يُّهِنِ اللّٰهُ فَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ مُّكْرِمٍ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَفْعَلُ مَا يَشَآءُ ۩  ؕ‏(18)\nALAM TARA ANNAL LAAHA YASJUDU LAHU MAN FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAN FIL ARZE WASH-SHAMSO WAL-QAMARO WA NOJOOMUN WA JEBAALO WASH-SHAJARO WAALDDAWAABBU WA KASEERUM MENAL NAASE WA KASEERUM HAQQA A’LAYHE A’ZAAB WA MAN YYUHENE LAAHO FAMAA LAHU MIN MMUKREMIN INNAL LAAHA YAF-A’LO MAA YASHAAA.\nSeest thou not that God (is He), unto Him prostrateth whosoever is in the heavens and whosoever is in the earth, and the sun and the moon and the stars and the mountains and the trees and animals, and many of the people; and many there are unto whom hath become due the chastisement; and whomsoever God abaseth, then there is none for him to honour; Verily God doeth whatever He willeth.\nهٰذٰنِ خَصْمٰنِ اخْتَصَمُوْا فِىْ رَبِّهِمْ‌ فَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا قُطِّعَتْ لَهُمْ ثِيَابٌ مِّنْ نَّارٍ ؕ يُصَبُّ مِنْ فَوْقِ رُءُوْسِهِمُ الْحَمِيْمُ‌ۚ‏(19)\nHAAZAANE KHASMAANE AKHTASAMOOA FEE RABBEHIM FAL LAZEENA KAFAROO QUTTEA’AT LAHUM SEEABUN MIN NAAR YUSABBU MIN FAWQE RUOOSEHEMU AL-HAMEEMU.\nThese are the two disputants who dispute about their Lord; but for those who disbelieved, shall be cut off for them garments of fire; (and) shall be poured over their heads boiling water.\nيُصْهَرُ بِهٖ مَا فِىْ بُطُوْنِهِمْ وَالْجُلُوْدُؕ‏(20)\nYUSHARU BEHI MAA FEE BOTOONEHIM WAL JULOODU.\nWith it shall be melted what is in their bellies and (their) skins (as well).\nوَلَهُمْ مَّقَامِعُ مِنْ حَدِيْدٍ‏(21)\nWA LAHUM MMAQAAMEU’U MIN HADEEDIN.\nAnd for them are maces of iron.\nكُلَّمَاۤ اَرَادُوْۤا اَنْ يَّخْرُجُوْا مِنْهَا مِنْ غَمٍّ اُعِيْدُوْا فِيْهَا وَذُوْقُوْا عَذَابَ الْحَرِيْقِ‏(22)\nKULLAMAA AARAADOOA AN YAKHROJOO MINHAA MIN GHAMMIN AUE’EEDOOA FEEHAA WA ZOOQOO A’ZAABAL AL-HAREEQE.\nEvery time they will intend to go forth from it, from the very anguish, back shall they be turned into it: and (it will be said unto them) “Taste ye the torment of the burning (fire).\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُدْخِلُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ يُحَلَّوْنَ فِيْهَا مِنْ اَسَاوِرَ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ وَّلُؤْلُؤًا ‌ؕ وَلِبَاسُهُمْ فِيْهَا حَرِيْرٌ‏(23)\nINNAL LAAHA YUDKHELU LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO YUHALLAWNA FEEHAA MIN ASAAWERA MIN ZAHABIN WWALULUAN WALEBAASUHUM FEEHAA HAREERUN.\nVerily, God will admit those who believe and do good deeds, into gardens ’neath which flow rivers, adorned shall they be therein with bracelets of gold and with pearls; and their raiment therein shall be of silk.\nوَهُدُوْۤا اِلَى الطَّيِّبِ مِنَ الْقَوْلِ‌ ۖۚ وَهُدُوْۤا اِلٰى صِرَاطِ الْحَمِيْدِ‏(24)\nWAHUDOOA ELAL AT-TAYBE MENAL AL-QAWLE WAHUDOOA ELAA SERAATE HAMEEDIL.\nFor they (in this life) are guided unto goodly words, and they are guided unto the path of the Praised One.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَيَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَالْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ الَّذِىْ جَعَلْنٰهُ لِلنَّاسِ سَوَآءَ اۨلْعَاكِفُ فِيْهِ وَالْبَادِ‌ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّرِدْ فِيْهِ بِاِلْحَادٍۢ بِظُلْمٍ نُّذِقْهُ مِنْ عَذَابٍ اَ لِيْمٍ‏(25)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WA YASUDDOONA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE WAL MASJEDIL HARAAME LAZEE LAW LIN-NAASE SAWAAA-AS AL-A’AAKEFU FEEHE WAL BAADE WA MAN YYURED FEEHE BEAELHAADIN BEZULMIN NNUZEQHU MIN A’ZAABIN A’ZAABAN LEEMIN.\nVerily, those who disbelieve and obstruct (people) from the way of God and from the Sacred Mosque (Masjid-al-Haram) which We have made alike; for the dweller therein as well as the stranger; and whoever doth intend to wrong therein unjustly, We will make him taste of a grievous chastisement.\nوَاِذْ بَوَّاْنَا لِاِبْرٰهِيْمَ مَكَانَ الْبَيْتِ اَنْ لَّا تُشْرِكْ بِىْ شَيْئًا وَّطَهِّرْ بَيْتِىَ لِلطَّآئِفِيْنَ وَالْقَآئِمِيْنَ وَ الرُّكَّعِ السُّجُوْدِ‏(26)\nWA IZ BAWANAA LE-IBRAAHEEMA MAKAANA BAYTE AN LAA TUSHREK BEE SHAY-ANW WWATAHHER BAYTEYA LIT-TAAA-EFEENA WAL QAAEMEENA WA AR-RUKKAE’E SOJOOD.\nAnd (remember O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) when We fixed for Abraham the place for the House, (saying): “Associate thou not with Me aught, and cleanse My House for those who make the circuits and stand in prayer, and bow and prostrate themselves (unto Me)\nوَاَذِّنْ فِى النَّاسِ بِالْحَجِّ يَاْتُوْكَ رِجَالًا وَّعَلٰى كُلِّ ضَامِرٍ يَّاْتِيْنَ مِنْ كُلِّ فَجٍّ عَمِيْقٍ ۙ‏(27)\nWAAZZEN FIL NAASE BE-HAJJE WA YAATOOKA REJAALAN WWAA’ALAA KULLE ZAAMERIN YAKHRUJNA MIN KULLE FAJJIN A’AMEEQIN.\nAnd proclaim thou unto the people the Pilgrimage (Hajj)! They will come unto thee on foot and on lean camel, coming from every remote (high) way.\nلِّيَشْهَدُوْا مَنَافِعَ لَهُمْ وَيَذْكُرُوا اسْمَ اللّٰهِ فِىْۤ اَ يَّامٍ مَّعْلُوْمٰتٍ عَلٰى مَا رَزَقَهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَهِيْمَةِ الْاَنْعَامِ‌‌ ۚ فَكُلُوْا مِنْهَا وَاَطْعِمُوا الْبَآئِسَ الْفَقِيْرَ‏(28)\nLLEESHHADOOA MANAAFEA’A LAHUM WAYAZKUROOA KORISMA LAAHE FEE A’ZAABAN YYAAMIN MMAA’LOOMAATIN A’LAA MAA RAZAQAHUM MIN BAHEEMATE AL-AANA’AAME FA-KOLOO MINHAA WAATE’EMOOA AL-BAAESA AL-FAQEERA.\nThat they may witness the advantages unto them, and mention the name of God during the appointed days over what He hath provided them of the cattle quadrupeds (as sustenance) then eat of them and feed the needy the poor.\nثُمَّ لْيَقْضُوْا تَفَثَهُمْ وَلْيُوْفُوْا نُذُوْرَهُمْ وَلْيَطَّوَّفُوْا بِالْبَيْتِ الْعَتِيْقِ‏(29)\nSUMMA LYAQZOOA TAFASAHUM WALYOOFOOA NUZOORAHUM WALYATTAWFOOA BE-BAYTE AL-A’ATEEQE.\nThen let them get cleansed and smarten themselves and fulfil their vows, and let them circuit the Ancient House (the Ka’ba).\nذٰلِكَ وَمَنْ يُّعَظِّمْ حُرُمٰتِ اللّٰهِ فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَّهٗ عِنْدَ رَبِّهٖ‌ؕ وَاُحِلَّتْ لَكُمُ الْاَنْعَامُ اِلَّا مَا يُتْلٰى عَلَيْكُمْ‌ فَاجْتَنِبُوا الرِّجْسَ مِنَ الْاَوْثَانِ وَاجْتَنِبُوْا قَوْلَ الزُّوْرِۙ‏(30)\nZAALEKA WA MAN YYUA’AZZEM HURUMAATE LAAHE FAHOWA KHAYRUL LAHU I’NDAL RABBEH WAAHELLAT LAKOMUL AL-AANA’AAMU ILLAA MAA YUTLAA A’LAYKUM FAAJTANEBOOA A’NKOMUR MENAL AL-AAWSAANE WAAJTANEBOOA QAWLA AZ-ZOORE.\nThat (shall be so); and whoever respecteth the sacred ordinances of God, it is best for him with his Lord; And the cattle are made lawful unto you, save that which is (already) specified unto you, shun ye therefore, the pollution of the idols; and shun vain words.\nحُنَفَآءَ لِلّٰهِ غَيْرَ مُشْرِكِيْنَ بِهٖ‌ؕ وَمَنْ يُّشْرِكْ بِاللّٰهِ فَكَاَنَّمَا خَرَّ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ فَتَخْطَفُهُ الطَّيْرُ اَوْ تَهْوِىْ بِهِ الرِّيْحُ فِىْ مَكَانٍ سَحِيْقٍ‏(31)\nHONAFAAA-A LILLAAHE GHAYRA MUSHREKEENA BEH WA MAN YYUSHREK BIL-LAAHE FAKAANNAMAA KHARRA MENAL SAMAAA-E FATAKHTAFUHU AT-TAYRU AW TAHWEAA BEHIL AR-REEHU FEE MAKAANIN SAHEEQIN.\nBeing upright for God, not associating (anything) with Him; whosoever associateth with God, is like that which hath fallen from heaven and (a vulture) bird snatched it away or the wind wafted it to a distant abyss.\nذٰلِكَ وَمَنْ يُّعَظِّمْ شَعَآئِرَ اللّٰهِ فَاِنَّهَا مِنْ تَقْوَى الْقُلُوْبِ‏(32)\nZAALEKA WA MAN YYUA’AZZEM SHAA’AAERA LAAHE FA INNAHAA MIN TAQWAA AL-QULOOBE.\nThat (shall be so); And whoever respecteth the signs of God verily it is (the reflection) of the piety of the hearts.\nلَكُمْ فِيْهَا مَنَافِعُ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى ثُمَّ مَحِلُّهَاۤ اِلَى الْبَيْتِ الْعَتِيْقِ‏(33)\nLAKUM FEEHAA MANAAFE-O’ ELAA ELAA AJALIM SUMMA MAHELLUHAA ELAL BAYTE AL-A’ATEEQE.\nFor you therein are benefits till a fixed time, and the place of their sacrifice is the Ancient House, (The Ka’ba).\nوَلِكُلِّ اُمَّةٍ جَعَلْنَا مَنْسَكًا لِّيَذْكُرُوا اسْمَ اللّٰهِ عَلٰى مَا رَزَقَهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَهِيْمَةِ الْاَنْعَامِ ؕ فَاِلٰهُكُمْ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ فَلَهٗۤ اَسْلِمُوْا‌ ؕ وَبَشِّرِ الْمُخْبِتِيْنَ ۙ‏(34)\nWA LEKULLIM UMMATIN JA-A’LNAA MANSAKAN LLEEZKUROOA KORISMA LAAHE A’LAA MAA RAZAQAHUM MIN BAHEEMATE AL-AANA’AAME FA ELAAHOKUM ELAAHUN WAAHED FALAHU AASLEMOOA WA BASH-SHERIL AL-MUKHBETEENA.\nUnto every people We have prescribed a rite (of devotion) that they may mention the name of God on what He hath provided them of the cattle quadrupeds, (as their sustenance) so your God is One God, so unto Him submit ye (all) yourselves; and thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) give glad tidings unto the humble ones,\nالَّذِيْنَ اِذَا ذُكِرَ اللّٰهُ وَجِلَتْ قُلُوْبُهُمْ وَالصّٰبِرِيْنَ عَلٰى مَاۤ اَصَابَهُمْ وَالْمُقِيْمِى الصَّلٰوةِ ۙ وَمِمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ يُنْفِقُوْنَ‏(35)\nLAZEENA EZAA ZUKERA LAAHO WAJELAT QULOOBUHUM WAS SAABEREENA A’LAA MAA AASAABAHUM WAL MUQEEMEAA AS-SALAAWTE WA MIMMAA RAZAQNAAHUM YUNFEQOONA.\nWho, when God is mentioned, get thrilled their hearts (with awe for His Glory); and the steadfast on what befalleth them, and the establishers of prayer and of what We have provided them with they spend (benevolently).\nوَالْبُدْنَ جَعَلْنٰهَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ شَعَآئِرِ اللّٰهِ لَكُمْ فِيْهَا خَيْرٌ‌ ‌ۖ  فَاذْكُرُوا اسْمَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهَا صَوَآفَّ‌ ۚ فَاِذَا وَجَبَتْ جُنُوْبُهَا فَكُلُوْا مِنْهَا وَاَطْعِمُوا الْقَانِعَ وَالْمُعْتَرَّ ‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ سَخَّرْنٰهَا لَكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(36)\nWAL BUDNA JA-A’LNAAHAA LAKUM MIN SHA-A’AA-ERIL LAAHE LAKUM FEEHAA KHAYRUL FAZKORUL KORISMA LAAHE A’LAYHAA SAWAAFFA FA-EZAA WAJABAT JUNOOBUHAA FA-KOLOO MINHAA WAATE’EMOOA AL-QAANEA’A WAL MUA’TARRA KAZAALEKA SAKKHARNAAHAA LAKUM LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nAnd the camels (of sacrifice) We have made them for you among the signs of God, for you in them is good; so mention the name of God on them (when they are drawn) in rows (to be sacrificed); and when fall they down (sacrificed), on their sides, eat of them and feed the contented (poor ones) and the beggar; thus have We subjugated them unto you that happly ye may give thanks.\nلَنْ يَّنَالَ اللّٰهَ لُحُوْمُهَا وَلَا دِمَآؤُهَا وَلٰكِنْ يَّنَالُهُ التَّقْوٰى مِنْكُمْ‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ سَخَّرَهَا لَكُمْ لِتُكَبِّرُوا اللّٰهَ عَلٰى مَا هَدٰٮكُمْ‌ؕ وَبَشِّرِ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(37)\nLAN YYANAALA LAAHA LUHOOMUHAA WA LAA DEMAAUHAA WA LAAKIL YYANAALUHU TAQWAA MENKUM KAZAALEKA SAKKHARAHAA LAKUM LETUKABBEROOA LAAHA A’LAA MAA HADAAKUM WA BASH-SHERIL MOHSENEEN.\nNever doth reach God their flesh nor their blood, but reacheth God the piety on your part; Thus hath He subjugated them unto you that ye might pronounce the greatness of God for what He hath guided you aright; and thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) give glad tidings unto the doers of good.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُدٰفِعُ عَنِ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْٓا‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُحِبُّ كُلَّ خَوَّانٍ كَفُوْرٍ‏(38)\nINNAL LAAHA YUDAAFEU’U A’NIL LAZEENA AAMANOO INNAL LAAHA LAA YOHIBBUL KULLA KHAWANIN KAFOORIN.\nVerily, God doth ward off (the mischief of infidels) from those who believe; Verily, God loveth not any of the unfaithful, ungrateful (ones).\nاُذِنَ لِلَّذِيْنَ يُقٰتَلُوْنَ بِاَنَّهُمْ ظُلِمُوْا‌ ؕ وَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى نَصْرِهِمْ لَقَدِيْرُ ۙ‏(39)\nAUZENA LILLAZEENA YUQAATALOONA BE-ANNAHUM ZULEMOOA WA INNA LAAHA A’LAA NASREHEM LAQADEERU.\nPermission (to fight) is given unto those upon whom war is made for they have been op pressed, and verily, to help them, God is Most Potent,\nاۨلَّذِيْنَ اُخْرِجُوْا مِنْ دِيَارِهِمْ بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّقُوْلُوْا رَبُّنَا اللّٰهُ‌ ؕ وَلَوْلَا دَ فْعُ اللّٰهِ النَّاسَ بَعْضَهُمْ بِبَعْضٍ لَّهُدِّمَتْ صَوَامِعُ وَبِيَعٌ وَّصَلَوٰتٌ وَّمَسٰجِدُ يُذْكَرُ فِيْهَا اسْمُ اللّٰهِ كَثِيْرًا‌ ؕ وَلَيَنْصُرَنَّ اللّٰهُ مَنْ يَّنْصُرُهٗ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَقَوِىٌّ عَزِيْزٌ‏(40)\nLAZEENA UKHREJOO MIN DEYAAREHIM BEGHAYRIL HAQQIN ILLAA AN YAQOOLOO RABBONAA LAAHO WA LAWLAA DA FU’U LAAHE NAASA BA’ZAHUM BE-BA’Z LLAHUDDEMAT SAWAAMEU’U WABEEA’UN WWASALAWTUN WWAMASAAJEDU YUZKARU FEEHAA RABBEKA LAAHE KASEERAA WALAYANSURANNA LAAHO MAN YYANSURUH INNAL LAAHA LAQAWIYYUN A’ZEEZUN.\nThose who have been expelled from their homes unjustly save that they say: “Our Lord is God!” And had repelled not God some people by others, verily had been pulled down the cloisters and the churches and the synagogues and the mosques in which is God’s name is much mentioned; and verily God will help him who helpeth Him (His cause); for verily God is Strong, Mighty.\nاَ لَّذِيْنَ اِنْ مَّكَّنّٰهُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ اَقَامُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتَوُا الزَّكٰوةَ وَاَمَرُوْا بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَنَهَوْا عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ‌ ؕ وَلِلّٰهِ عَاقِبَةُ الْاُمُوْرِ‏(41)\nA’ZAABAN LLAZEENA IN MMAKKANNAAHUM FIL ARZE AAQAAMOOA SALAATA WA AATAWUZ ZAKAATA WAAMAROOA BIL-MA’ROOF WANAHAWA A’NIL AL-MUNKARE LILLAAHE A’AQEBATUL AL-AUMOORE.\nThose, if We establish them in the earth, will establish prayer and pay the poor-rate and enjoin good and forbid evil; and unto God (alone) is the sequel of (all) affairs,\nوَاِنْ يُّكَذِّبُوْكَ فَقَدْ كَذَّبَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ قَوْمُ نُوْحٍ وَّعَادٌ وَّثَمُوْدُ ۙ‏(42)\nWA YYUKAZZEBOOKA FAQAD KAZZABAT QABLAHUM QAWMO NOOHIN WWAA’AADUN WWASAMOODU.\nAnd if they belie thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) then indeed have belied before thee the people of Noah and ’Ad and Thamud (the prophets sent unto them),\nوَقَوْمُ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَقَوْمُ لُوْطٍ ۙ‏(43)\nWA QAWMO IBRAAHEEMA WA QAWMO LOOTIM.\nAnd the people of Abraham and the people of Lot\nوَّاَصْحٰبُ مَدْيَنَ‌ۚ وَكُذِّبَ مُوْسٰى فَاَمْلَيْتُ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ ثُمَّ اَخَذْتُهُمْ‌ۚ فَكَيْفَ كَانَ نَكِيْرِ‏(44)\nWWAASHAABU MADYANA WAKUZZEBA MOOSAA FAAMLAYTU LIL KAAFEREENA SUMMA AAKHAZTUHUM FA-KAYFA KAANA NAKEER.\nAnd the dwellers of Midian, and was (also) belied Moses, but gave I respite unto the disbelievers, then I did seize them, and how (severe) was My (wrathful) rejection.\nفَكَاَيِّنْ مِّنْ قَرْيَةٍ اَهْلَكْنٰهَا وَهِىَ ظَالِمَةٌ فَهِىَ خَاوِيَةٌ عَلٰى عُرُوْشِهَا وَبِئْرٍ مُّعَطَّلَةٍ وَّقَصْرٍ مَّشِيْدٍ‏(45)\nFAKAAYYEN MIN QARYATINW AAHLAKNAAHAA WA HEYA ZAALEMATUN FAHEYA KHAAWEYATUN A’LAA O’ROOSHEEHAA WABERIN MMUA’ATTALATIN WWAQASRIN MMASHEEDIN.\nSo how many of towns We did destroy while they were un just, and (their walls) have fallen down over their roofs, and (how many a) well abandoned and (even) lofty castles (ruined)\nاَفَلَمْ يَسِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَتَكُوْنَ لَهُمْ قُلُوْبٌ يَّعْقِلُوْنَ بِهَاۤ اَوْ اٰذَانٌ يَّسْمَعُوْنَ بِهَا‌ ۚ فَاِنَّهَا لَا تَعْمَى الْاَبْصَارُ وَلٰكِنْ تَعْمَى الْقُلُوْبُ الَّتِىْ فِى الصُّدُوْرِ‏(46)\nA-FALAM YASEEROO FIL ARZE FA TAKOONA LAHUM QULOOBUN YA’QELOON BEHAA AW AAAZAANUN YASMA-O’ON BEHAA FA INNAHAA LAA TAA’MAA IZ ZAAGHATIL WA LAAKIL TAA’MAA BALAGHATIL LATEE FIL SODOOR.\nWhat! Have not they travelled in the earth that they should have hearts to understand them with, or ears to hear them with? for verily blind are not the eyes but blind are the hearts which are in the breasts.\nوَيَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَكَ بِالْعَذَابِ وَلَنْ يُّخْلِفَ اللّٰهُ وَعْدَهٗ‌ ؕ وَاِنَّ يَوْمًا عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ كَاَ لْفِ سَنَةٍ مِّمَّا تَعُدُّوْنَ‏(47)\nWA YASTA’JELOONAKA BE-A’ZAABE WA LAN YUKHLEFAL LAAHO WA’DAHU WA INNA YAWMAN I’NDAL RABBEKA KA-A’ZAABAN LFE WA MIMMAA TAU’UDDOONA.\nAnd they ask thee to hasten on the chastisement and never doth God fail His promise; And verily, there is a day with thy Lord as a thousand years, of what ye reckon (them).\nوَكَاَيِّنْ مِّنْ قَرْيَةٍ اَمْلَيْتُ لَهَا وَهِىَ ظَالِمَةٌ ثُمَّ اَخَذْتُهَا‌ۚ وَاِلَىَّ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(48)\nWA KA-AYYIM MIN QARYATINW AAMLAYTU LAHAA WA HEYA ZAALEMATUN SUMMA AAKHAZTUHAA WA ELAYYA MASEER.\nAnd how many a town I did give a respite unto it while it was unjust, then I did seize it; and unto Me is the return.\nقُلْ يٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اِنَّمَاۤ اَنَا لَكُمْ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‌ۚ‏(49)\nQUL YAA AYYOHAL NAASO INNAMAA ANAA LAKUM NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\nSay: thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) O’ ye people, I am unto you only an Open Warner;\nفَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَ عَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ لَهُمْ مَّغْفِرَةٌ وَّرِزْقٌ كَرِيْمٌ‏(50)\nFAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE LAHUM MAGHFERATUNW WWAREZQUN KAREEM.\nThen (as for) those who believe and do good, for them is pardon and an honourable provision.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ سَعَوْا فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِنَا مُعٰجِزِيْنَ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(51)\nWAL LAZEENA SAA’AWA FEE AAYAATENAA MUA’AAJEZEENA OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN JAHEEM.\nAnd those who strive to invalidate Our signs they shall be the inmates of the flaming (Hell) fire.\nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِكَ مِنْ رَّسُوْلٍ وَّلَا نَبِىٍّ اِلَّاۤ اِذَا تَمَنّٰٓى اَلْقَى الشَّيْطٰنُ فِىْۤ اُمْنِيَّتِهٖ ‌ۚ فَيَنْسَخُ اللّٰهُ مَا يُلْقِى الشَّيْطٰنُ ثُمَّ يُحْكِمُ اللّٰهُ اٰيٰتِهٖ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ ۙ‏(52)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA MIN QABLEKA MIN RASOOLIN WA LAA NABEAAAIN ILLAA EZAA TAMANNAAA AALQAA SHAYTAANO FEE AUMNEETEH FAYANSAKHU LAAHO MAA YULQEAA SHAYTAANO SUMMA YUHKEMU LAAHO AAYAATEHI WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nAnd We sent not before thee (O’ Our Apostle Muham mad!) any apostle or prophet, but when he recited (the message) the Satan did cast his recitation (to create error); But annulleth God that which the Satan casteth, then God doth establish His signs; And verily God is All-Knowing, All-Wise,\nلِّيَجْعَلَ مَا يُلْقِى الشَّيْطٰنُ فِتْنَةً لِّلَّذِيْنَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌ وَّالْقَاسِيَةِ قُلُوْبُهُمْ‌ ۚ وَ اِنَّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ لَفِىْ شِقَاقٍۭ بَعِيْدٍۙ‏(53)\nLLEEJA’ALA MAA YULQEAA SHAYTAANO FETNATAN LIL-LAZEENA FEE QOLOOBEHIM MARAZUN WWAALQAASEETE QULOOBUHUM WA INNAL ZAALEMEEN LAFEE SHEQAAQIM BA-E’ED.\nSo that he may make that which casteth the Satan a trial unto those in whose hearts is disease and those whose hearts are hard; and verily, the unjust are in a schism far (away from the truth),\nوَّلِيَعْلَمَ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ اَنَّهُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ فَيُؤْمِنُوْا بِهٖ فَتُخْبِتَ لَهٗ قُلُوْبُهُمْ‌ ؕ وَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَهَادِ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(54)\nWWALEEA’LAMA LAZEENA OOTUL OOTUL I’LMA ANNAHUL HAQQO MIN RABBEKA FA YOAMENOO BEHI FATUKHBETA LAHU QULOOBUHUM WA INNA LAAHA LAHAADE LAZEENA AAMANOO ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nAnd that may know those who have been given the knowledge that it (Qur’an) is the truth from thy Lord, so they may believe in it and may humble unto it their hearts; and verily, God guideth those who believe, unto the right path.\nوَلَا يَزَالُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا فِىْ مِرْيَةٍ مِّنْهُ حَتّٰى تَاْتِيَهُمُ السَّاعَةُ بَغْتَةً اَوْ يَاْتِيَهُمْ عَذَابُ يَوْمٍ عَقِيْمٍ‏(55)\nWA LAA YAZAALU LAZEENA KAFAROO FEE MIRYATIM MINHO HATTAA TAA-TEYAHOMUL SAA-A’TO BAGHTATANW AW YAATEEHUM A’ZAABO YAWMIN A’AQEEMIN.\nAnd will cease not those who disbelieve, in (their) doubt about it (Qur’an) until overtaketh them the Hour (of Resurrection) suddenly, or cometh unto them the doom of the day of desolation.\nاَ لْمُلْكُ يَوْمَئِذٍ لِّلَّهِ ؕ يَحْكُمُ بَيْنَهُمْ‌ ؕ فَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَ عَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ فِىْ جَنّٰتِ النَّعِيْمِ‏(56)\nA’ZAABAN LMULKU YAWMA-EZIN LILLAAH YAHKOMO BAYNAHUM FAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE FEE JANNATIN NA-E’EM.\nThe Kingdom that day shall be God’s; He will judge between them; and those who believe and do good will be in the gardens of bliss.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا فَاُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مُّهِيْنٌ‏(57)\nWAL LAZEENA KAFAROO WA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA FA-OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM A’ZAABUN MOHEEN.\nAnd those who disbelieve and belie Our signs, these, for them shall be a chastisement disgraceful.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هَاجَرُوْا فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ثُمَّ قُتِلُوْۤا اَوْ مَاتُوْا لَيَرْزُقَنَّهُمُ اللّٰهُ رِزْقًا حَسَنًا‌ؕ وَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَهُوَ خَيْرُ الرّٰزِقِيْنَ‏(58)\nWAL LAZEENA HAAJAROO FEE SABEELIL LAAHE SUMMA QUTELOOA AW MAATOOA LAYARZUQANNAHUMU LAAHO RIZQAN HASANAN WA INNA LAAHA LAHOWAL KHAYRUR RAAZEQEEN.\nAnd those who migrate in the Way of God and are then slain or die, certainly will God provide them with an excellent sustenance; and Verily, God is the Best of providers.\nلَيُدْخِلَنَّهُمْ مُّدْخَلًا يَّرْضَوْنَهٗ‌ ؕ وَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَعَلِيْمٌ حَلِيْمٌ‏(59)\nLAYUDKHELANNAHUM MMUDKHALAN YYARZAWNAH WA INNA LAAHA LAA’ALEEMUN HALEEM.\nCertainly, will He admit them into an entrance which they shall be well pleased with; Verily, God is the All-Knowing, the Most Forbearing.\nذٰ لِكَ‌ۚ وَمَنْ عَاقَبَ بِمِثْلِ مَا عُوْقِبَ بِهٖ ثُمَّ بُغِىَ عَلَيْهِ لَيَنْصُرَنَّهُ اللّٰهُ ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَعَفُوٌّ غَفُوْرٌ‏(60)\nZAA LEKA WA MAN A’AAQABA BE-MISLE MAA U’OOQEBA BEHI SUMMA BUGHEAAA A’LAYHE LAYANSURANNAHU LAAHO INNAL LAAHA LAA’AFOO GHAFOORUR.\nThat (shall be so); and he who did retaliate with the like of that which he hath been wronged, and again he hath been aggressed, most certainly God will aid him; Verily God is the Most Merciful, Oft-Forgiving.\nذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّ اللّٰهَ يُوْلِجُ الَّيْلَ فِى النَّهَارِ وَيُوْلِجُ النَّهَارَ فِى الَّيْلِ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ سَمِيْعٌۢ بَصِيْرٌ‏(61)\nZAA LEKA BE-ANNAL LAAHA YOOLEJU LAYLA FIL AN-NAHAARE WAYOOLEJU NAHAARA FIL LAYLE WA ANNAL LAAHA SAMEE-U’N BASEER.\nThat is because God causeth the night to enter into the day and causes the day to enter into the night, and because God is All-Seeing, All-Hearing.\nذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الْحَقُّ وَاَنَّ مَا يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ هُوَ الْبَاطِلُ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الْعَلِىُّ الْكَبِيْرُ‏(62)\nZAA LEKA BE-ANNAL LAAHA HOWA HAQQO WA ANNAL MAA YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONEHI HOWA BAATELO WA ANNAL LAAHA HOWA A’LIYYUL AL-KABEERU.\nThat is because God, He is the Truth and that what they call upon besides Him - it is falsehood, and because God, He is the Highest, the Great.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ اَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً  فَتُصْبِحُ الْاَرْضُ مُخْضَرَّة ً  ؕاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَطِيْفٌ خَبِيْرٌ‌ ۚ‏(63)\nALAM TARA ANNAL LAAHA ANZALAL MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FATUSBEHU ARZO MUKHZARRAT AENNA LAAHA LATEEFUN KHABEERUM.\nSeest thou not that God sendeth down from the heaven water and (by it) the earth becometh green? Verily God is Benign, Subtle, All-Aware.\nلَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ‌ ؕ وَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَهُوَ الْغَنِىُّ الْحَمِيْدُ‏(64)\nLAHU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE WA INNA LAAHA LAHOWAL AL-GHANEAAAU AL-HAMEEDU.\nHis is whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is in the earth; Verily God, certainly He is the Self-Sufficient, The Praised One.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ سَخَّرَ لَكُمْ مَّا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَالْفُلْكَ تَجْرِىْ فِى الْبَحْرِ بِاَمْرِهٖ ؕ وَيُمْسِكُ السَّمَآءَ اَنْ تَقَعَ عَلَى الْاَرْضِ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِهٖ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِالنَّاسِ لَرَءُوْفٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(65)\nALAM TARA ANNAL LAAHA SAKKHARA LAKUM MAA FIL ARZE WAL FULKA TAJREE FIL BAHRE LAAHO WAYUMSEKU SAMAAA-AD AN TAQAA’A A’LAL ARZE ILLAA BE-IZNEH INNAL LAAHA BIN-NAASE LA-RAOOFUR RAHEEM.\nSeest thou not that God hath subjugated for thee whatsoever is in the earth and the ships sailing in the sea by His command? And He withholdeth the heaven that it falleth not on the earth, save with His permission; Verily, God unto the people is Compassionate, All-Merciful.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَحْيَاكُمْ ثُمَّ يُمِيْتُكُمْ ثُمَّ يُحْيِيْكُمْ‌ ؕ اِنَّ الْاِنْسَانَ لَكَفُوْرٌ‏(66)\nWA HOWA LAZEE AAHYAAKUM SUMMA YOMEETOKUM SUMMA YOHYEEKUM INNAL INSAANA LAKAFOORUN.\nAnd He it is who hath brought you to life (for the first time), then He will cause you to die, then bring you to life (again); Verily man is ungrateful.\nلِّكُلِّ اُمَّةٍ جَعَلْنَا مَنْسَكًا هُمْ نَاسِكُوْهُ‌ فَلَا يُنَازِعُنَّكَ فِى الْاَمْرِ‌ وَادْعُ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ‌ ؕ اِنَّكَ لَعَلٰى هُدًى مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(67)\nLEKULLE UMMATIN JA-A’LNAA MANSAKAN HUM NAASEKOOHU FALAA YUNAAZEU’UNNAKA FIL AL-AAMRE WAD-O’ ELAA RABBEKA INNAKA LAA’ALAA HODAM MUSTAQEEM.\nUnto every people have We prescribed the rites of devotion which they observe, so they should dispute not with thee about the affair, and call thou unto thy Lord; Verily, thou art on the Right way.\nوَاِنْ جَادَلُوْكَ فَقُلِ اللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(68)\nWA JAADALOOKA FA QOLIL LAAHO A-A’LAMO BEMAA TA’MALOON.\nAnd if they dispute with thee, say thou: “God knoweth best what ye do.\nاللّٰهُ يَحْكُمُ بَيْنَكُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فِيْمَا كُنْتُمْ فِيْهِ تَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(69)\nLAAHO YAHKOMO BAYNAKUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE FEEMAA KUNTUM FEEHE TAKHTALEFOONA.\nGod will judge between you on the Day of Judgment wherein ye differ.\nاَلَمْ تَعْلَمْ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ مَا فِى السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ اِنَّ ذٰ لِكَ فِىْ كِتٰبٍ‌ ؕ اِنَّ ذٰ لِكَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ يَسِيْرٌ‏(70)\nALAM TA’LAM ANNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO MAA FIL SAMAAA-E WAL ARZ INNAL ZAA LEKA FEE KETAABIM INNAL ZAA LEKA A’LAL LAAHE YASEERUN.\nKnowest thou not that God knoweth what is in the heaven and the earth? Verily this is in the Book (of the Divine Will); Verily this is easy for God.\nوَيَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَمْ يُنَزِّلْ بِهٖ سُلْطٰنًا وَّمَا لَيْسَ لَهُمْ بِهٖ عِلْمٌ‌ؕ وَمَا لِلظّٰلِمِيْنَ مِنْ نَّصِيْرٍ‏(71)\nWA YA’BODOON MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAM YUNAZZEL BEHI SULTAANAN WA MAA LAYSA LAHUM BEHI E’ELMUN WA MAA LIZ-ZAALEMEENA MIN NNASEERIN.\nAnd worship they besides God that for which He hath sent not any authority, and that of which they have no knowledge; and there shall not be for the unjust any helper.\nوَاِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتُنَا بَيِّنٰتٍ تَعْرِفُ فِىْ وُجُوْهِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا الْمُنْكَرَ‌ ؕ يَكَادُوْنَ يَسْطُوْنَ بِالَّذِيْنَ يَتْلُوْنَ عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتِنَا‌ ؕ قُلْ اَفَاُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِشَرٍّ مِّنْ ذٰ لِكُمُ‌ ؕ اَلنَّارُؕ وَعَدَهَا اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا‌ ۚ وَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(72)\nWA EZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHIM AAYAATONAA BAYYENAAT TA’REFO FEE WUJOOHE LAZEENA KAFAROO NAADEEKOMUL YAKAADOONA YASTOONA BE-LAZEENA YATLOONAL A’LAYHIM AAYAATENAA QUL AAFAANABBEUKUM BESHARRIN MIN ZAA LEKUMU AALNNAARU WAA’ADAHAA LAAHO LAZEENA KAFAROO WA BEASAL MASEER.\nAnd when are recited Our clear signs unto them, thou wilt perceive repugnance on the faces of those who disbelieve; they well nigh spring upon those who recite unto them Our signs; Say thou: “Shall I inform you of what is worse than this? The “Fire”; God hath promised it unto those who disbelieve; How evil is the resort!\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ ضُرِبَ مَثَلٌ فَاسْتَمِعُوْا لَهٗ ؕ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ لَنْ يَّخْلُقُوْا ذُبَابًا وَّلَوِ اجْتَمَعُوْا لَهٗ‌ ؕ وَاِنْ يَّسْلُبْهُمُ الذُّبَابُ شَيْئًا لَّا يَسْتَنْقِذُوْهُ مِنْهُ‌ ؕ ضَعُفَ الطَّالِبُ وَالْمَطْلُوْبُ‏(73)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO ZUREBA MASALUN FAASTAMEU’OOA LAHU INNAL LAZEENA TADU’OONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE LAN YYAKHLUQOOA ZUBAABAN WWALAWE AJTAMAU’OOA LAHU WA YYASLUBHUMU AZ-ZUBAABU SHAY-ANW LAA YASTANQEZOOHU MINHO ZAU’UFA AT-TAALEBU WAL MATLOOBU.\nO’ ye people! A parable is set forth (unto you) so listen ye unto it! Verily, those whom ye call upon besides God can never create (even) a fly, even though they all gather (themselves) together for it; and should the fly carry away any thing from them, they can not take it back from it; (how) weak the invoker and the invoked!\nمَا قَدَرُوا اللّٰهَ حَقَّ قَدْرِهٖؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَقَوِىٌّ عَزِيْزٌ‏(74)\nMAA QADAROOA LAAHA HAQQA QADREH INNAL LAAHA LAQAWIYYUN A’ZEEZUN.\nThey estimated not God His rightful estimation; Verily, God is All-Strong, and All-Mighty.\nاَللّٰهُ يَصْطَفِىْ مِنَ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةِ رُسُلًا وَّمِنَ النَّاسِ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَمِيْعٌۢ بَصِيْرٌ ‌ۚ‏(75)\nALLAAHO YASTAFEAA MENAL MALAA-EKATE ROSOLAN WWAMENA NAAS INNAL LAAHA SAMEE-U’N BASEER.\nGod chooseth from among the angels messengers and from among the men; Verily God is All-Hearing, All-Seeing.\nيَعْلَمُ مَا بَيْنَ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَمَا خَلْفَهُمْ‌ؕ وَاِلَى اللّٰهِ تُرْجَعُ الْاُمُوْرُ‏(76)\nYA’LAMO MAA BAYNA AYDEEHIM WA MAA KHALFAHUM WA ELAL LAAHE TURJA-U’L OMOOR.\nKnoweth He what is before them and what is behind them, and unto God are returned all affairs.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا ارْكَعُوْا وَاسْجُدُوْا وَ اعْبُدُوْا رَبَّكُمْ وَافْعَلُوْا الْخَيْرَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَ۩ ۚ‏(77)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO ARKAU’OOA WA JODOO WA BODOO TAQUL WAAFA’ALOOA AL-KHAYRA LA-A’LLAKUM TUFLEHOON.\nO’ ye who believe! Bow ye down and prostrate ye and worship ye your Lord, and do ye good, happly ye may succeed.\nوَجَاهِدُوْا فِى اللّٰهِ حَقَّ جِهَادِهٖ‌ؕ هُوَ اجْتَبٰٮكُمْ وَمَا جَعَلَ عَلَيْكُمْ فِى الدِّيْنِ مِنْ حَرَجٍ‌ؕ مِلَّةَ اَبِيْكُمْ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ‌ؕ هُوَ سَمّٰٮكُمُ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ ۙ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَفِىْ هٰذَا لِيَكُوْنَ الرَّسُوْلُ شَهِيْدًا عَلَيْكُمْ وَتَكُوْنُوْا شُهَدَآءَ عَلَى النَّاسِ‌ ‌ۖۚ فَاَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتُوا الزَّكٰوةَ وَاعْتَصِمُوْا بِاللّٰهِؕ هُوَ مَوْلٰٮكُمْ‌ۚ فَنِعْمَ الْمَوْلٰى وَنِعْمَ النَّصِيْرُ‏(78)\nWAJAAHEDOOA FIL LAAHE HAQQA JEHAADEH HOWA AJTABAAKUM WA MAA JA-A’LA A’LAYKUM FIL DEENE MIN HARAJIN MILLATA AABEEKUM AEBRAAHEEMA HOWA SAMMAAKUMU AKOONA MENAL MUSLEMEEN MIN QABLO WA FEE HAAZAA LEYAKOONA RASOOLO SHAHEEDAA A’LAYKUM WA TAKOONOO SHOHADAAA-A A’LAL NAASE FAAQEEMOOA SALAATA WA AATUZ ZAKAATA WAAA’TASEMOOA BILLAAH HOWA MAWLAAKUM FA NE’MA AL-MAWLAA WA NE’MA AN-NASEERU.\nAnd fight (endeavour) ye in (the way of) God as it behoveth you to fight (endeavour) for Him; He hath chosen you and hath laid not upon you any hardship in religion; The faith of your Father Abraham; He (God Himself) named you Muslims before and in this, that the Apostle may be a witness over you and ye be witness over the people; So establish ye prayer and pay ye the poor-rate and hold ye fast by God; He is your Master - How Excellent the Master and How Excellent the Helper!",
  "merits": "Surah al-Hajj (The Pilgrimage)\nThere are 78 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that reciting this Surah carries the reward equal to the number of pilgrims who have been for Hajj and those who will go for Hajj in the future.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that whoever recites this Surah once in every three days will get the opportunity of going for Hajj in the same year, and if he dies on the way, he will be granted Paradise. Someone asked what would happen if the person performing the Hajj was a sinner, so the Imam (a.s.) replied that his punishment would be reduced."
